&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;📍London or Remote (UK) | 💰£80,000 - £105,000 +&lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers/&quot;&gt; Benefits&lt;/a&gt; |&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Business Banking at Monzo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since its launch five years ago, Monzo Business Banking has been dedicated to delivering the very best of Monzo to small businesses. Today, it&#39;s an award-winning service, empowering over 1 million businesses across the UK.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Monzo expands across Europe, Business Banking is entering its next phase: adapting our products and proposition for small businesses in new markets, while continuing our mission to make money work for businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for &lt;em&gt;several&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Senior PMMs &lt;/strong&gt;to own Product Marketing for entire products and experiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A useful distinction - at Monzo, Product Marketing starts upstream in product-market fit. We&#39;re embedded in squads with Product Managers, Data Scientists, Designers, User Researchers, and Sales, bringing the voice of the customer and market into what we build, how we position it, and how we take it to market. We own customer and market understanding, positioning, proposition, launch strategy, and sales enablement. We then partner closely with Integrated Marketing, who lead campaign strategy, creative direction, channel execution, and growth. Together, we build the right products and help them succeed in market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll own Product Marketing for a product end-to-end: understanding customers, shaping product strategy, defining positioning, and helping bring launches to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you could join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Banking EU. &lt;/strong&gt;Business Banking is entering its next phase of growth as we expand beyond the UK. In this role, you&#39;ll define how Monzo Business Banking succeeds in new European markets - understanding local customer needs, building the proposition that translates our core product into local relevance, and working across Product, Growth, Marketing, and local teams to bring those products to market. This is a senior role for someone with high autonomy who loves turning dense customer and market insight into practical decisions about what should launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Banking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;. &lt;/strong&gt;Business Banking is growing quickly, serving more than one million businesses across the UK while expanding into increasingly sophisticated customer needs. In this role, you&#39;ll shape how our products are positioned, sold, and adopted—from defining compelling product narratives to enabling Sales and partnering with Growth and Marketing on launches. This is a role for someone who enjoys sitting at the intersection of Product and commercial teams, translating customer insight into positioning, propositions, and go-to-market strategies that help more businesses choose Monzo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set Product Marketing Strategy for a set of products. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ll define a one-year Product Marketing strategy for a major area of Business Banking, connecting customer insight, market opportunity, and commercial priorities into a clear direction for the product area, rather than one individual product, with measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop differentiated positioning &amp;amp; messaging: &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ll create compelling positioning, messaging, and value propositions that differentiate Monzo in the market and resonate with different customer segments. You&#39;ll build messaging frameworks that Product, Sales, Integrated Marketing, and broader marketing teams use consistently across launches and customer journeys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive competitive intelligence and market insights&lt;/strong&gt;: You’ll build and maintain the market view for your product area. You&#39;ll become the recognised authority on your customer segment and competitive landscape, building a coherent view of the market from customer research, commercial data, competitor intelligence, and Sales insight. Your recommendations will shape product strategy, positioning, go-to-market, and commercial priorities across the Business Banking collective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape product strategy across markets.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll partner closely with Product, Research, Design, and Data to identify customer problems, market opportunities, and competitive gaps that influence roadmap priorities. Your customer and market insight will shape what we build, not just how we bring it to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the go-to-market strategy for priority products and markets&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll define what audiences we prioritise, why they would choose Monzo, what needs to be true for them to switch and stay, and what success looks like - giving Product, Sales, Marketing, and local market teams a shared strategic direction for how the product enters or scales in market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own product representation across the customer journey.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll define the core proposition and value messages that should carry through key customer and sales touchpoints, so customers consistently understand why the product matters. You&#39;ll partner with teams across Product, Sales, Marketing, CRM, and local markets to make sure the customer experience reflects the agreed positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable localisation:&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll work with local market teams to determine what should remain globally consistent and what should adapt locally, ensuring positioning, customer journeys, and launches resonate in each market while strengthening the overall Monzo Business Banking proposition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is for you if: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re recognised for your Product Marketing expertise.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re comfortable owning Product Marketing across a product area or market, and people seek your perspective on customers, competitors, positioning, and product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You bring senior stakeholders with you &amp;amp; thrive in cross-functional environments. &lt;/strong&gt;You work effectively across Product, Sales, Growth, Marketing, and Research, building alignment around difficult decisions and helping teams make confident product and commercial choices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You raise the quality of the work around you.&lt;/strong&gt; You enjoy mentoring less experienced PMMs, sharing your expertise, and improving how the team works through better frameworks, feedback, and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Interview Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our interview process involves three main stages:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initial Call (45mins)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Case Study Presentation (1hour)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;x2 final interviews via Google Meet (45mins for each interview)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This process should take around 3-4 weeks - your schedule is really important to us, so we promise to be as flexible as possible!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have some guidelines on using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to ace an application and interview at Monzo. &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-on-using-ai-to-ace-an-interview-at-monzo&quot;&gt;You can read them here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll hear from us throughout the application process, but if you’ve got any questions, please reach out to ----- You can also use this email address to let us know if there’s anything we can do to make the process easier for you because of disability, neurodiversity or anything else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;£80,000 - £105,000 as a base salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will be based out of our London office next to Liverpool Street station in a hybrid approach of office based and home working, or remotely within the UK&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, at times that suit you and your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning budget of £1,000 a year for books, training courses and conferences&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And much more, see our full list of benefits &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers#benefits&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ll only close this role once we have enough applications for the next stage. Please submit your application as soon as possible to make sure you don’t miss out.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-JB1 #LI-REMOTE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunities for everyone&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Diversity and inclusion are a priority for us and we’re making sure we have lots of support for all of our people to grow at Monzo. At Monzo, we’re embracing diversity by fostering an inclusive environment for all people to do the best work of their lives with us. This is integral to our mission of making money work for everyone. You can read more in our &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/diversity-and-inclusion&quot;&gt;blog&lt;/a&gt;, 2026 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/our-2026-diversity-and-inclusion-report&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Diversity and Inclusion Report&lt;/a&gt; and 2025 &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/gender-pay-gap-report-2025&quot;&gt;Gender Pay Gap Report.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer. All applicants will be considered for employment without attention to age, ethnicity, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, or veteran, neurodiversity or disability status.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a preferred name, please use it to apply. We don&#39;t need full or birth names at application stage 😊&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IonQ:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2F&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=IonQ%2C+Inc&amp;amp;index=7&amp;amp;md5=0818ffbedc6dbad8c4d1611ac94c2a0f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;IonQ, Inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;. [NYSE: IONQ] is the world’s leading quantum platform and merchant supplier - delivering integrated quantum solutions across computing, networking, sensing, and security. IonQ’s newest generation of quantum computers, the IonQ Tempo, is the latest in a line of cutting-edge systems that have been helping customers and partners including &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=Amazon+Web+Services%2C&amp;amp;index=8&amp;amp;md5=a7f94ee9b71a392dca3cd6c413722e51&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Amazon Web Services, &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=and&amp;amp;index=9&amp;amp;md5=2bed627b388878763f41ffe0e4edb16c&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;and &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-speeds-quantum-accelerated-drug-development-application-with&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=AstraZeneca&amp;amp;index=10&amp;amp;md5=757c1f2c2ec94cf3982700106122164f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AstraZeneca&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt; achieve 20x performance results and accelerate innovation in drug discovery, materials science, financial modeling, logistics, cybersecurity, and defense. In 2025, the company achieved 99.99% two-qubit gate fidelity, &lt;u&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://cts.businesswire.com/ct/CT?id=smartlink&amp;amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fionq.com%2Fnews%2Fionq-achieves-landmark-result-setting-new-world-record-in-quantum-computing&amp;amp;esheet=54451094&amp;amp;newsitemid=20260316477473&amp;amp;lan=en-US&amp;amp;anchor=setting+a+world+record+in+quantum+computing+performance&amp;amp;index=11&amp;amp;md5=32e9cb88afbd439026a352666cc72c91&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;setting a world record in quantum computing performance&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Headquartered in College Park, Maryland, IonQ has operations in California, Colorado, Massachusetts, Tennessee, Washington, Italy, South Korea, Sweden, Switzerland, Canada, and the United Kingdom. Our quantum computing services are available through all major cloud providers, while we also meet the needs of networking and sensing customers across land, sea, air, and space. IonQ is making quantum platforms more accessible and impactful than ever before. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Oxford Ionics, now part of IonQ, we are building the first practical quantum computer. Our systems are based on ion traps, which hold individual atomic ions tens of microns above the surface of a chip, and we design and build them in house, bringing together optomechanics, vacuum and cryogenic technology, electronics and system infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Mechanical Engineer to join our Systems team and take ownership of mechanical design from first requirements through to manufacture and integration. You will work on the hardware that surrounds the quantum processor, including cryostat requirements, cooling equipment, vacuum chambers and supporting structures, often in areas where the requirements are not yet fully defined.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work alongside scientists, technicians and the wider hardware design teams to bring new systems through to manufacture. That means producing CAD designs, bills of materials and assembly drawings, managing documentation in our PLM system and working with suppliers and our manufacturing team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our manufacturing team handles most assembly, but you will support technicians in the lab, investigate problems when they arise and make sure your designs can be built in practice. The work ranges from complex system layout to simple brackets and documentation, and you will see each piece through to completion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanically integrate multiple sub systems into one complete system, driving the overall mechanical layout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce 3D designs of system assemblies and infrastructure, with detailed 2D drawings and bills of materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design systems for vacuum pump down, gas handling and coolant management lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan the routing of cables, optical fibre and other physical services throughout the system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather and scope requirements with scientists and engineers, then roll out upgrades and variations to system builds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be a mechanical engineer with a strong design background and a practical understanding of how things are assembled and manufactured. A degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field, or equivalent experience, and around five years of relevant industry experience will give you the grounding the role needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want someone proactive who asks questions, gathers requirements, spots the missing details and sees a job through. You will be comfortable working independently with a high degree of autonomy, while collaborating closely with scientists and engineers across disciplines. Quantum experience is not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’d be a great fit with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established CAD ability, ideally in SolidWorks, with a focus on assembly structure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of complex multidisciplinary systems and good assembly practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cryogenic or vacuum systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GD&amp;amp;T and preparing drawings for manufacture and inspection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of PLM systems or thermal analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The total compensation package includes base salary, bonus, equity, and a range of benefits available on our career site.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Compensation will vary based on individual factors such as education, qualifications, and experience of the final candidate(s), specific office location, and calibration against relevant market data and internal team equity. Posted base salary figures are subject to change as new market data becomes available. Our benefits include comprehensive medical, dental, and vision plans, matching 401(k), unlimited PTO and paid holidays, parental/adoption leave, legal insurance, and a home technology stipend. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided when a candidate receives an offer of employment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IonQ, we believe in fair treatment, access, opportunity, and advancement for all while striving to identify and eliminate barriers. We empower employees to thrive by fostering a culture of autonomy, productivity, and respect. We are dedicated to creating an environment where individuals can feel welcomed, respected, supported, and valued.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to equity and justice. We welcome different voices and viewpoints and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, ancestry, physical and/or mental disability, medical condition, genetic information, marital status, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, transgender status, age, sexual orientation, military or veteran status, or any other basis protected by law. We are proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;The position you are applying for will require access to technology that is subject to U.S. export control and government contract restrictions.&amp;nbsp; Employment with IonQ is contingent on either verifying “U.S. Person” (e.g., U.S. citizen, U.S. national, U.S. permanent resident, or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum) status for export controls and government contracts work, obtaining any necessary license, and/or confirming the availability of a license exception under U.S. export controls.&amp;nbsp; Please note that in the absence of confirming you are a U.S. Person for export control and government contracts work purposes, IonQ may choose not to apply for a license or decline to use a license exception (if available) for you to access export-controlled technology that may require authorization, and similarly, you may not qualify for government contracts work that requires U.S. Persons, and IonQ may decline to proceed with your application on those bases alone.&amp;nbsp; Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;US Non-Technical Jobs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Due to applicable export control laws and regulations, candidates must be a U.S. citizen or national, U.S. permanent resident (i.e., current Green Card holder), or lawfully admitted into the U.S. as a refugee or granted asylum. Accordingly, we will have some additional questions regarding your immigration status that will be used for export control and compliance purposes, and the answers will be reviewed by compliance personnel to ensure compliance with federal law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in being a part of our team and mission, we encourage you to apply!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Commercial Finance Business Partner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;284&quot; data-end=&quot;599&quot;&gt;The Commercial Planning team sits at the heart of SumUp&#39;s commercial engine, turning complex data into the financial insight that shapes how we grow. We partner closely with Sales leaders and commercial teams to make sure our planning is accurate, proactive, and genuinely useful to the people making decisions.&amp;nbsp;In this role, you’ll primarily support our Sales function, owning analytical and planning workstreams while acting as a trusted finance partner to Sales leadership. If you&#39;re energised by owning complex models, understanding what drives sales performance, influencing commercial decisions, and being the person stakeholders turn to when they need clarity, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end revenue and customer acquisition budget (CAB) planning for acquisition channels, building scalable financial models, running scenario analyses, and delivering proactive performance insights to senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a primary finance business partner to Sales and commercial leaders, building trusted relationships, embedding financial models into decision-making, and using data to challenge assumptions and identify opportunities to improve performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct deep-dive analyses at country, merchant category, and channel level to surface revenue risks and opportunities, and present findings clearly to senior, non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build business cases and product-level revenue forecasts to support existing and new product growth initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the migration of commercial planning from spreadsheets to scalable forecasting tools, and help reduce manual effort in month-end reporting workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day guidance to an intern and/or analyst, helping them develop their skills and navigate complex analytical tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience acting as a primary finance business partner to Sales and commercial leaders, building trusted relationships, embedding financial models into decision-making, and using data to challenge assumptions and identify opportunities to improve performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level financial modelling skills, including multi-driver models and scenario analysis, with advanced proficiency in Excel or Google Sheets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;4vcvp8&quot; data-start=&quot;2115&quot; data-end=&quot;2270&quot;&gt;Proven ability to act as a trusted finance business partner, comfortable challenging and influencing Sales leaders and senior commercial stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of SQL for data extraction and manipulation from large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and structured communicator, able to translate complex analysis into sharp, actionable insight for senior non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in fast-moving environments where priorities shift, and structure is still being built&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our central London Bridge location, wrapped in historic charm and modern flair. This involves an office-first setup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏖 Generous time off: enjoy 28 days of paid leave, plus bank holidays and special leaves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget for attending conferences and/or advancing your career through further education&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏥 Health matters: private health insurance, including optical and dental&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚗 Life made easier: salary-sacrifice commuter benefits via Gogeta&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💼 Financial security: retirement scheme (SumUp matches 7% when you contribute 5%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🛡 Peace of mind: life insurance from MetLife for 2× your salary&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About SumUp&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be empowered to do more that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, we&#39;re on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 39 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in our diverse team of over 3,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset. Our core values lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don&#39;t make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our careers website, and follow our journey on LinkedIn, Instagram, and TikTok.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Established in 2004, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;OLIVER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; is the world’s first and only specialist in designing, building, and running bespoke in-house agencies and marketing ecosystems for brands. We partner with over 300 clients in 40+ countries and counting. Our unique model drives creativity and efficiency, allowing us to deliver tailored solutions that resonate deeply with audiences.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;As a part of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The Brandtech Group&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;, we&#39;re at the forefront of leveraging cutting-edge AI technology to revolutionise how we create and deliver work. Our &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;AI solutions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; enhance efficiency, spark creativity, and drive insightful decision-making, empowering our teams to produce innovative and impactful results.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Role: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Global Programme Director&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt; London, United Kingdom &lt;strong&gt;(1-3 days a week from our London HQ)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;THE OPPORTUNITY&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;OLIVER is growing — and we&#39;re building our pipeline of senior programme talent ahead of new account wins across our global network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking to connect with experienced Global Programme Directors who are open to an early conversation about upcoming opportunities. As we pitch for and win major international accounts, we want to hear from programme leaders who thrive in complex, multi-region environments and have a consistent track record of delivering at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;This isn&#39;t a specific vacancy. It&#39;s an invitation to start a conversation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Based in London, with a hybrid working pattern (1–3 days in our London offices), these roles sit at the intersection of strategic direction, commercial leadership, and operational excellence. We support flexible working and are open to discussing different arrangements. We offer reasonable adjustments throughout our process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Global Programme Directors at OLIVER are the most senior programme voice on their accounts — trusted by clients at executive level and accountable for delivery health, financial performance, and team capability across everything they touch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll lead medium-to-complex, multi-region programmes, bringing together creative, production, technology, and commercial disciplines to deliver transformational outcomes for some of the world&#39;s most ambitious brands. You&#39;ll drive measurable change within one of the most innovative in-house agency models in the industry — and help shape what programme excellence looks like across OLIVER&#39;s global network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme Delivery and Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead medium-to-complex global programmes, maintaining alignment to strategic goals, financial targets, and client expectations throughout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and drive programme vision — managing organisational change and delivering integrated outcomes across studios, functions, and geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold full accountability for delivery health: governance, risk management, issue resolution, and stakeholder coordination across concurrent workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and track KPIs; produce regular programme status reports covering risks, issues, and performance metrics; implement corrective actions as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead enterprise-scale transformation programmes centred on technology, people, and process — mapping dependencies, managing timelines, and ensuring nothing falls between workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold full accountability for account gross profit, including all approvals that affect GP: resourcing decisions, freelancers, expenses, and ad hoc cost requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build complex scenario plans across multiple brands and regions, modelling the impact of tools, technology, and commercial decisions on programme performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and manage Corrective Action Plans to protect GP targets; make strategic adjustments to people and cost base as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present revenue forecasting and financial performance to COO, SVP, and executive stakeholders; secure business approvals on decisions with financial implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cost efficiency across tightly resourced teams — identifying and implementing appropriate levers without compromising output quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical and Solution Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep fluency across OLIVER and BTG technology and services, including delivery platforms, automation tools, and AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead senior-level client conversations on technical solutions — knowing when to resolve directly and when to bring in specialist expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design solutions that integrate commercial thinking, people resources, and technology to meet client needs at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Senior Leadership Team on solution packaging and client proposals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource and Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee resource scheduling and utilisation across account portfolios, ensuring people are deployed efficiently and workloads are balanced across the wider OLIVER network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Client Services and Resource Management on pipeline planning to ensure team structure is correctly sized and skilled at each stage of delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure clear RACI frameworks are in place across all disciplines; confirm reporting lines and accountabilities are understood across the programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop programme teams — providing leadership, mentoring, and structured feedback that raises capability and performance at every level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;A strong track record of leading global programme delivery across large-scale, multi-studio account portfolios in complex organisational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Ideally Advertising/ Marketing industry experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Deep expertise in programme and project management — including governance, risk management, delivery health, and stakeholder coordination across multiple concurrent workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Advanced commercial acumen — experience managing large-scale budgets with direct accountability for gross profit, revenue forecasting, and financial performance reporting to executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Executive-level client partnership experience — building and sustaining trusted relationships with senior clients, managing escalations, and leading strategic conversations with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Proven ability to lead and develop large, geographically distributed teams — creating accountability, clarity, and high performance across diverse disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Experience leading enterprise-scale transformation programmes centred on technology, people, and process change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Fluency with delivery management platforms and operational tools, including Agile and scrum methodologies. Familiarity with automation and AI platforms is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Ability to design commercially viable solutions that integrate people, technology, and process — and to partner with senior leadership on how those solutions are packaged and communicated to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;A clear track record of meeting and protecting GP targets across complex, multi-region accounts, including experience presenting financial performance and forecasting to COO and SVP-level stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gen AI and Agentic Thinking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic integration of AI and automation across programme delivery and studio operations — identifying where these tools create measurable efficiency and quality gains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting AI governance and quality standards at programme or studio level, ensuring responsible and effective adoption across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of developing AI capability across multiple teams and disciplines, embedding new ways of working into programme operations and client delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic leadership for complex, multi-stakeholder business challenges — systematic and goal-oriented in approach to problem-solving at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thought leadership on AI&#39;s evolving role in agency operations, contributing to best practice internally and with clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial and Budget Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing programme-level budgets at significant scale, with accountability for gross profit, scenario planning, corrective action planning, and strategic cost management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence presenting budget performance and financial forecasting to senior and executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;Qualifications: Formal qualifications are welcome but not required. Equivalent experience counts — gained through work, study, or professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;If you&#39;re excited about where OLIVER is heading and don&#39;t meet every point above, we still encourage you to get in touch.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our values shape everything we do:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Be&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; Ambitious&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; to succeed &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Imaginative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; to push the boundaries of what’s possible &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Inspirational&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; to do groundbreaking work &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;always learning and listening&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; to understand &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Results-focused &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;to exceed expectations &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Be &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;actively pro-inclusive and anti-racist&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; across our community, clients and creations  &lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Our recruitment process does not employ artificial intelligence for selection. We use AI to support efficiency and consistency, not to replace human judgement.&amp;nbsp;Candidate evaluation and selection are conducted without AI-supported screening or decision-making. We are committed to a fair, thoughtful, and equitable experience for every candidate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;OLIVER,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;a part of the Brandtech Group, is an equal opportunity employer committed to creating an inclusive working environment where all employees are encouraged to reach their full potential, and individual differences are valued and respected. All applicants shall be considered for employment without regard to race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, neurodivergence, disability status, or any other characteristic protected by local laws. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; OLIVER has set ambitious environmental goals around sustainability, with science-based emissions reduction targets. Collectively, we work towards our mission, embedding sustainability into every department and through every stage of the project lifecycle.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your wellbeing, our mission. Join a company shaping a healthier world.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GET TO KNOW US&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Wellhub we&#39;re revolutionizing workplace wellness. Our platform connects employees worldwide to the best partners for fitness, mindfulness, therapy, nutrition, and sleep—all in one simple subscription. Headquartered in NYC with team members in Europe, North America and South America, we’re on a mission to make every company a wellness company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe work should be fulfilling, inspiring, and balanced. Here, you’ll find a team that values wellbeing, collaboration, and different perspectives, where passion and creativity push boundaries to create real impact. Your contributions will help shape a healthier, more balanced world for you and millions of people globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us in redefining the future of wellbeing!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Fitness Partner Sales Representative to our Partner Sales team in London!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you passionate about health, fitness, and wellness? Do you have experience in the health and fitness sector? Join a team of like-minded individuals and help us make every company a wellness company. We’re looking for a talented and ambitious Partner Sales Representative to join our UK &amp;amp; Ireland Partnerships team in London, focusing on growing our partner portfolio and driving overall growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR IMPACT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research, identify, and tenaciously target new opportunities via various forms and channels of communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect from initial contact to partnership agreement and network launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop creative and innovative ways to connect with potential fitness partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high volume of activity, including cold calls, emails, and social media through various outreach tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide consistent follow-up through different stages of the sales cycle using provided tech tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for consistently reaching and exceeding your daily KPI metrics, as well as your monthly sales quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive on change while remaining highly organized, optimistic, and coachable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Live the mission: inspire and empower others by genuinely caring for your own wellbeing and your colleagues. Bring wellbeing to the forefront of work, and create a supportive environment where everyone feels comfortable taking care of themselves, taking time off, and finding work-life balance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO YOU ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must reside in London with availability to go to the office at least twice a week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2 years experience in outbound sales role where you owned the sales process from initial outreach to close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outgoing and enthusiastic conversationalist with strong phone presence and perseverance comfortable with cold calling as well as multiple other communication touchpoints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work a high volume of leads in a fast paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing expectations and overcoming objections with leads and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Positive attitude that thrives in a team setting while also owning your accountability for individual motivation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills and ability to demonstrate an organized workflow and funnel management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of SaaS sales or Wellness Management Software is desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We recognize that individuals approach job applications differently. We strongly encourage all aspiring applicants to go for it, even if they don’t match the job description 100%. We welcome your application and will be delighted to explore if you could be a great fit for our team. For this specific role, please note that prior experience in Customer Success or sales, and residing in London, are mandatory requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER YOU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With thoughtful benefits, emotional wellbeing resources, and a culture that empowers you to take ownership of your role and your wellbeing, we create an environment where you can thrive in all dimensions of your life. Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WELLHUB:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; Free Gold membership with access to onsite gyms and studios, digital fitness programs, and online wellness resources for meditation, nutrition, mental wellbeing support, and more! Add up to three family members to your plan, ensuring access to wellness for those who matter most to you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HEALTHCARE:&lt;/strong&gt; Health and dental insurance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLEXIBLE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt; As a Flexible First company, we offer hybrid and remote options to give you the freedom to work in a way that suits you. The model for this specific role can be discussed with your recruiter and hiring manager. We offer all employees a one-time reimbursement to set up their home office equipment and a monthly work allowance to help cover the costs of working from home.&amp;nbsp;Our offices are in Germany, Italy, Netherlands, Portugal, Romania, Spain, and the UK. You can work from any office or remotely based in any of these countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLEXIBLE SCHEDULE: &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Flexibility for us isn’t just about where we work—it also means being able to shape how and when we get things done. Together with their leaders, employees define schedules that align with their time zones, team needs, and personal routines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PAID TIME OFF:&lt;/strong&gt; We know how important it is to take time away from work to recharge. Employees receive a minimum of 25 days paid holiday per year with an additional day for each year of tenure (up to 5) in addition to annual holidays (including an extra holiday on your birthday!).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PARENTAL LEAVE:&lt;/strong&gt; Welcoming a new child is one of the most special moments in your life. Take the time to be present and enjoy your growing family. We offer 100% paid parental leave to all new parents. Parents giving birth are eligible for an extended leave and a ramp-back period to return part-time while they get settled.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CAREER GROWTH:&lt;/strong&gt; Access world-class platforms, participate in interactive sessions,&amp;nbsp; build your personalized development roadmap, and explore internal opportunities. We focus on continuous learning and feedback to support your journey toward personal and professional success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CULTURE:&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll join a team of passionate people who come together to break boundaries, support each other, and create a meaningful impact in workplace wellness. We win together, building trust through open communication and a culture where every perspective matters. &lt;a href=&quot;https://wellhub.com/en-us/careers/our-values/&quot;&gt;Learn more about our shared culture and values here.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Want to see what it’s really like to work here? Follow us on &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/lifeatwellhub/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instagram&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; @lifeatwellhub and watch our team video on &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZgIPiszTVm4&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YouTube&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity, and Belonging at Wellhub&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We aim to create a collaborative, supportive, and inclusive space where everyone knows they belong.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wellhub is committed to creating a diverse work environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, religion, color, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, non-disqualifying physical or mental disability, national origin, veteran status, or any other basis covered by appropriate law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to inclusion also extends to how we recognize and reward our people. We’re proud to be Syndio Fair Pay Certified, reflecting our ongoing dedication to equitable and fair pay practices across our global team. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/posts/wellhub_fairpay-syndio-activity-7407826561531363328-wbN_?utm_source=share&amp;amp;utm_medium=member_desktop&amp;amp;rcm=ACoAAAzHQWABKsRqcpvxy4QpDCJNe_szRdC4hgY&quot;&gt;Read more about it here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Questions on how we treat your personal data? See our &lt;a href=&quot;https://wellhub.com/en-us/careers/job-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Notice.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
